{"id": "ccp6", "code": "CCP6", "label": "Scripts & automatisation", "questions": [{"n": 1, "title": "Variables Bash", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Quelle commande affiche la valeur de la variable <code>$USER</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>print $USER</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>echo $USER</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>display $USER</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>show $USER</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 2, "title": "Redirection de sortie", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Que fait la commande <code>ls /home &gt; liste.txt</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Affiche liste fichiers et crée fichier vide"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Écrit sortie <code>ls</code> dans liste.txt (écrase si existe)"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Ajoute sortie <code>ls</code> à la fin de liste.txt"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Provoque une erreur"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 3, "title": "Permissions fichiers", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Que signifie <code>chmod 755 script.sh</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Propriétaire: rwx, Groupe: r-x, Autres: r-x"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Tous: lecture seule"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Propriétaire: rw-, Groupe: r--, Autres: r--"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Erreur de syntaxe"}], "answer": ["A"]}, {"n": 4, "title": "Shebang", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Quelle ligne doit être en première ligne d'un script Bash ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code># Bash script</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>#!/bin/bash</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>&lt;bash&gt;</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>@echo off</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 5, "title": "Test condition", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Quelle syntaxe teste si fichier existe ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>if exist fichier.txt</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>if [ -f fichier.txt ]</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>if test fichier.txt</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>if (-e fichier.txt)</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 6, "title": "Boucle for", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Que fait ce code : <code>for i in 1 2 3; do echo $i; done</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Affiche <code>1 2 3</code> sur une ligne"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Affiche 1, 2, 3 chacun sur nouvelle ligne"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Erreur de syntaxe"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Affiche <code>i</code> 3 fois"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 7, "title": "Paramètres script", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Dans un script, que contient <code>$1</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Nom du script"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Premier argument passé au script"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Premier processus lancé"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Nombre d'arguments"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 8, "title": "Commande grep", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Que fait <code>grep \"erreur\" /var/log/syslog</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Supprime lignes contenant \"erreur\""}, {"l": "B", "html": "Affiche lignes contenant \"erreur\""}, {"l": "C", "html": "Compte occurrences \"erreur\""}, {"l": "D", "html": "Remplace \"erreur\" par \"\""}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 9, "title": "Pipe (tube)", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Que fait <code>cat fichier.txt | wc -l</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Affiche contenu et nombre de mots"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Compte nombre de lignes dans fichier.txt"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Compte caractères"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Erreur syntaxe"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 10, "title": "Condition if/else", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">if [ $age -ge 18 ]; then\n  echo &quot;Majeur&quot;\nelse\n  echo &quot;Mineur&quot;\nfi\n</code></pre>\n<p>Que teste <code>-ge</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Égal à"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Supérieur ou égal"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Inférieur strict"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Différent de"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 11, "title": "Variable spéciale", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Que contient <code>$?</code> après exécution commande ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "PID processus"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Code retour dernière commande (0=succès)"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Nombre arguments"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Nom utilisateur"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 12, "title": "Substitution commande", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Quelle syntaxe stocke résultat <code>date</code> dans variable ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>ma_date = date</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>ma_date=$(date)</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>ma_date = $(date)</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>$ma_date=date</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 13, "title": "Lecture entrée utilisateur", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Quelle commande demande saisie utilisateur ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>input nom</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>read nom</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>scan nom</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>get nom</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 14, "title": "Condition AND", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<p>Quelle syntaxe exécute cmd2 SI cmd1 réussit ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>cmd1 &amp;&amp; cmd2</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>cmd1 || cmd2</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>cmd1 &amp; cmd2</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>cmd1 ; cmd2</code>"}], "answer": ["A"]}, {"n": 15, "title": "Fonction Bash", "section": "PARTIE 1 : BASH", "html": "<pre><code class=\"language-bash\">ma_fonction() {\n  echo &quot;Hello $1&quot;\n}\nma_fonction &quot;World&quot;\n</code></pre>\n<p>Que affiche ce code ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>Hello</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>Hello $1</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>Hello World</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Erreur"}], "answer": ["C"]}, {"n": 16, "title": "Variables PowerShell", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Quelle syntaxe déclare variable PowerShell ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>var $nom = \"valeur\"</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>$nom = \"valeur\"</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>set nom = \"valeur\"</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>let $nom = \"valeur\"</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 17, "title": "Cmdlets", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Quel est le format standard cmdlets PowerShell ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>Action.Object</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>Verbe-Nom</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>nom_action</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>ActionNom</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 18, "title": "Pipeline PowerShell", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Que fait <code>Get-Process | Where-Object {$_.CPU -gt 10}</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Liste tous processus"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Liste processus avec CPU &gt;10 secondes"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Arrête processus CPU &gt;10"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Erreur syntaxe"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 19, "title": "Alias", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Quel alias correspond à <code>Get-ChildItem</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>list</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>dir</code> et <code>ls</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>show</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>cat</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 20, "title": "Comparaison", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Quel opérateur teste égalité (case insensitive) ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>==</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>-eq</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>-equal</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>=</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 21, "title": "Boucle ForEach", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">$names = @(&quot;Alice&quot;, &quot;Bob&quot;)\nforeach ($name in $names) {\n  Write-Host $name\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Que affiche ce code ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>Alice Bob</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Alice puis Bob (2 lignes)"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>$name</code> 2 fois"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Erreur"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 22, "title": "Condition If", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">if ($age -ge 18) {\n  &quot;Majeur&quot;\n} else {\n  &quot;Mineur&quot;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Quelle différence avec <code>Write-Host</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Aucune"}, {"l": "B", "html": "String seule retourne objet (peut être stocké)"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Erreur syntaxe"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Write-Host obligatoire"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 23, "title": "Paramètres fonction", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">function Get-Square {\n  param([int]$nombre)\n  return $nombre * $nombre\n}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Comment appeler cette fonction ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>Get-Square 5</code> ou <code>Get-Square -nombre 5</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>Get-Square(5)</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>Get-Square $5</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>Square 5</code>"}], "answer": ["A"]}, {"n": 24, "title": "Gestion erreurs", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Quelle structure capture erreurs PowerShell ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>if/else</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>try/catch</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>error/handle</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>check/fail</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 25, "title": "Objets PowerShell", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Que fait <code>Get-Service | Select-Object Name, Status</code> ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Affiche tous services"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Affiche uniquement colonnes Name et Status"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Filtre services actifs"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Renomme colonnes"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 26, "title": "Import module", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Comment importer module Active Directory ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>Load-Module ActiveDirectory</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>Import-Module ActiveDirectory</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>Use-Module ActiveDirectory</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>Get-Module ActiveDirectory</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 27, "title": "Commentaires", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Quelle syntaxe pour commentaire PowerShell ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>// commentaire</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code># commentaire</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>&lt;!-- commentaire --&gt;</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>/* commentaire */</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 28, "title": "Types de données", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Quelle commande force conversion string → int ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "<code>$nombre = int(\"42\")</code>"}, {"l": "B", "html": "<code>$nombre = [int]\"42\"</code>"}, {"l": "C", "html": "<code>$nombre = convert(\"42\", int)</code>"}, {"l": "D", "html": "<code>$nombre = ToInt(\"42\")</code>"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 29, "title": "Exécution script", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<p>Pourquoi erreur \"cannot be loaded because running scripts is disabled\" ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Script corrompu"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Execution Policy restrictive"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Droits insuffisants"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Syntaxe incorrecte"}], "answer": ["B"]}, {"n": 30, "title": "Sélection propriétés calculées", "section": "PARTIE 2 : POWERSHELL", "html": "<pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">Get-Process | Select-Object Name,\n  @{Name=&quot;MemMB&quot;;Expression={$_.WS/1MB}}\n</code></pre>\n<p>Que fait cette commande ?</p>", "options": [{"l": "A", "html": "Erreur syntaxe"}, {"l": "B", "html": "Affiche nom processus + mémoire en MB"}, {"l": "C", "html": "Filtre processus &gt;1MB"}, {"l": "D", "html": "Renomme propriété WS"}], "answer": ["B"]}], "eval": "../../CCP6-Scripts-Automatisation/QCM/Evaluation/QCM-CCP6-Scripting-30Q/", "correction": "../../CCP6-Scripts-Automatisation/QCM/Correction/QCM-CCP6-Scripting-30Q-CORRECTION/"}